      en: "Beacon Island (Île Sèche) is a small uninhabited island off Mahé, designated as a nature reserve in 1992. Spanning 5 hectares, it hosts breeding colonies of sooty terns, noddies, and other seabirds, with a population exceeding 10,000 birds. The island is a crucial stopover for migratory birds. Research on avian populations is ongoing. Access is restricted to minimize disturbance. Boat tours allow wildlife observation. It is part of Seychelles' protected area network.",
